<title>UK: Slovakia to award mandate for dollar bond - bankers.</title>
<headline>Slovakia to award mandate for dollar bond - bankers.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Slovakia is expected to launch a $250 million five-year Eurobond in July, bankers said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The mandate was expected to be announced this week.</p>
<p>&quot;Slovakia has asked for formal bids, the bids went in last week and there will be a decision made imminently...they're ready to go,&quot; a syndicate manager at a European bank said.</p>
<p>The country is rated BBB- by Standard &amp; Poor's. Price</p>
<p>talk was 75 basis points over U.S. Treasury notes.</p>
<p>In February the Slovak Finance Ministry said it was considering an international bond to help cover budget expenditures.</p>
<p>-- Hayley Pienaar, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7718</p>
